125-## [3] CORE CONCEPTS
126-
127-### 3.1 Grounding Need
128:Grounding Need exists when the answer materially depends on evidence not already dependable in the active context.
129-
130-### 3.2 Evidence Target
131:Evidence Target is the minimum evidence standard required to support the intended claim strength.
132-
133-### 3.3 Provenance
134:Provenance is the inspectable source lineage of a claim, including where the evidence came from and why it was trusted.
135-
136-### 3.4 Freshness Boundary
137-Freshness Boundary is the degree to which time sensitivity matters for correctness.
138-
139-### 3.5 Evidence Coverage
140:Evidence Coverage is the extent to which the acquired evidence adequately supports the important parts of the answer.
141-
142-### 3.6 Source Conflict Trigger
143-Source Conflict Trigger occurs when retrieved sources materially disagree and the disagreement could change the answer or recommendation.
144-
145-### 3.7 Citation-Grounded Synthesis
146:Citation-grounded synthesis is synthesis that remains tied to actual retrieved evidence rather than conclusion-first paraphrasing.
147-
148-### 3.8 Agentic RAG
149:Agentic RAG is a retrieval mode in which a reasoning layer actively evaluates source quality, resolves contradictions, decomposes complex evidence needs, and may invoke additional retrieval or external tools when justified.
150-
151-### 3.9 Evidence Pack
152-An Evidence Pack is the minimized set of retrieved material passed into answer generation or downstream processing.
153-
154-### 3.10 Composite Evidence
155:Composite evidence is support assembled from multiple distinct fragments or sources because no single source sufficiently covers the claim.
156-
157-### 3.11 Currentness
158-Currentness is the justified confidence that a retrieved source reflects the relevant present state rather than historical or stale context.
--
166-`Detect Grounding Need -> Define Evidence Target -> Check Freshness Boundary -> Select Retrieval Mode -> Acquire Evidence -> Rank and Filter -> Slice Minimal Evidence -> Check Coverage and Conflict -> Build Evidence Pack -> Synthesize with Provenance -> Cite or Surface Limitation -> Stop or Escalate`
167-
168-Decision rules:
169:- do not retrieve before identifying what must be evidenced
