776:### 25A. Operational artifact governance
777-
778-When retrieval failure diagnosis rather than answer synthesis is the main issue:
779-- prefer a `Context substrate scorecard` over a lighter taxonomy memo when omissions, overload, provenance drift, or stale context must be scored
780-- keep `stale context`, `provenance drift`, `freshness defect`, and `late clarification` independently visible rather than smoothing them into generic retrieval weakness
781:- if repeated context defects are claimed, preserve `scenario_id`, `run_id`, `cohort_id`, `trace_id`, and `artifact_version` so the defect can be reviewed longitudinally
782:- before joining substrate scorecards with broader evidence packets, check precedence, compatibility, freshness, and completeness; reject incompatible merges that would overstate grounding strength
783:- preserve upstream source IDs and `artifact_version` in any joined retrieval artifact that survives reconciliation
