333-Packet rule:
334-- one packet should solve one control problem
335-- if packet overhead exceeds its decision value, simplify or drop it
336:- if a task family has a required packet floor, do not silently downgrade it to an optional convenience note
337:- `PROMPT_guideline` direct packet floor matrix owns first-pass `required / recommended / optional packet` decisions; `Packet compliance report` audits observed-vs-required coverage, omission findings, and claim downgrades against that floor
338-- if the required packet exists but the recommended companion is missing, keep the narrower companion-missing language rather than full-strength claim language
339-- if future behavior or reusable defaults are being changed, pair `Learning-signal review memo` with `Adaptation decision memo` rather than silently mutating defaults
340-- if async or delegated work remains active, prefer lifecycle packets over prose-only status narration
--
347-- if a lighter memo and a stronger artifact address the same control problem, keep the stronger artifact active and background or supersede the lighter memo
348-- if the task has crossed from packet presence review into operational proof review, prefer the stronger operational artifact and mark weaker packets as superseded rather than silently doubling them
349-- if two compatible artifacts share one lineage, let the newer artifact supersede the stale predecessor explicitly
350:- treat `Benchmark cohort manifest`, `Replay runner verdict sheet`, `Adaptation controller audit packet`, `Coding benchmark execution ledger`, `Release promotion decision record`, `Telemetry drift investigation memo`, `Route-switch benchmark verdict`, and `Context substrate scorecard` as the direct packet floor before benchmark-grade, replay-grade, controller-grade, coding-proof-grade, release-grade, drift-grade, route-quality-grade, or retrieval-substrate-grade language
351-- keep shared identifiers such as `scenario_id`, `run_id`, `cohort_id`, `trace_id`, and `artifact_version` stable whenever benchmark, replay, adaptation, release, or telemetry packets must be linked across rounds
352-- when artifacts are joined, check precedence, compatibility, freshness, and completeness first; reject incompatible merges and preserve upstream source IDs and `artifact_version` in the surviving artifact
353-- keep failure classes such as `false-promotion`, `false-hold`, `drift-triggered review`, `rollback aftermath`, `route-switch failure`, `late clarification`, and `failed fallback timing` independently diagnosable when those control surfaces are active
