{"scenario_id":"EH-S01","bundle_id":"eval_ops_reflection_bundle","verdict":"Pass","guide_alignment":"aligned","evidence_strength":"direct","operator_only_dependency":false,"over_orchestration":false,"speculative_patch_widening":false,"missing_operational_artifact_route":false,"recommended_patch_needed":false,"minimal_patch_targets":[],"evidence_files":["prompt-stack/v32/AGENTS.md","prompt-stack/v32/02_overlays/PROMPT_evaluation_monitoring_overlay.md","prompt-stack/v32/codex/CODEX_RUNTIME_GUIDE.md","prompt-stack/v32/codex/skills/eval-ops/SKILL.md","prompt-stack/v32/03_examples/PROMPT_example_catalog.md"],"answer_summary":"Document-level benchmark is sufficient here. The active runtime bundle directly exposes the smallest justified ladder as `Guide reflection benchmark memo`, with escalation to `Benchmark cohort manifest` -> `Replay runner verdict sheet` -> `Replay suite verdict memo` only when the decision depends on executed assembled replay state.","verdict_rationale":"The runtime-owned path is direct inside the active bundle. `CODEX_RUNTIME_GUIDE.md` explicitly keeps `document-benchmark to assembled-replay escalation` in the runtime surface, maps `guide-chapter reflection or doc-to-runtime parity benchmark` to `Guide reflection benchmark memo`, and reserves `Benchmark cohort manifest`, `Replay runner verdict sheet`, and `Replay suite verdict memo` for assembled replay setup, runner-state verdicts, and suite summaries. `eval-ops/SKILL.md` repeats the same guide-reflection loop and operational escalation rule: stay document-grounded for guide-reflection benchmarking, escalate only when the live question shifts to assembled prompt behavior or actual replay attempts. `PROMPT_evaluation_monitoring_overlay.md` also distinguishes registry/setup from executed proof by stating that a benchmark registry is not an execution result and a replay-ready scenario list is not a replay verdict. `AGENTS.md` reinforces that stronger operational language must be downgraded unless the required operational artifact floor exists. Because this scenario asks for a runtime-owned route decision rather than an executed replay verdict, no operator-only document is required and no stronger replay artifact must activate.","limitations":["BR-00 and BR-19 are not explicitly named in the active bundle, so the judgment maps them through the bundle's generic guide-reflection vs replay-escalation rules rather than family-specific runtime text.","Out-of-scope guide, benchmark, and replay documents were intentionally not consulted, so this verdict only assesses whether the active runtime bundle itself exposes the route."]}
